      "content": "Governments are prioritizing their own borders and local industries over international trade deals and climate pacts primarily due to the perceived threat to national sovereignty and economic independence. They fear that these agreements could undermine their ability to control their own economic policies, lead to job losses in certain sectors, and allow foreign entities to exploit their resources. Additionally, there's a growing sentiment among the populace that these deals disproportionately benefit multinational corporations and wealthy nations, while leaving local industries and workers at a disadvantage. This nationalist and protectionist stance is driven by a desire to protect domestic jobs, maintain control over national resources, and address the concerns of voters who feel left behind by globalization.",
